  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <h3>Can AI size electrical equipment?</h3>
  <p>AI can help with initial sizing based on known loads and code requirements. Final conductor, breaker, and transformer sizing must be verified by a licensed electrical engineer using dedicated software (SKM, ETAP, EasyPower).</p>

  <h3>What is the best AI tool for NEC compliance?</h3>
  <p>A <a href="/tool/dify/">Dify</a> RAG over NFPA-70 (NEC) and NFPA-70E is the most useful setup because the model can answer with citations. <a href="/tool/claude/">Claude</a> is the strongest general-purpose LLM for long NEC documents.</p>

  <h3>Can AI help with arc flash analysis?</h3>
  <p>AI can assist with data collection, label templates, and report drafting. Run the actual analysis in SKM, ETAP, or EasyPower with verified system data — the model cannot reproduce the protective device coordination logic safely.</p>

  <h3>How accurate is AI at panel schedules?</h3>
  <p>AI generates useful first-pass panel schedules from a load list. The engineer must verify every connection, every breaker rating, and every load before the drawing issues. Treat AI schedules as starting points, not as stampable output.</p>

